"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"No smoking or drinking at all throughout pregnancy — and no one else in the house should smoke either"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"For women at high risk of preeclampsia, start taking one low-dose aspirin tablet daily after week 12 of pregnancy"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Get screened for gestational diabetes at 24 weeks of gestation or later — don’t mind drinking the sugary solution"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Memorize this “go to the hospital immediately” checklist — it applies throughout pregnancy and the first year after childbirth"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"If your water breaks, lie down flat, elevate your hips, and call 120 — don’t walk around or take a shower"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Ask for labor analgesia — it does not raise the risk of C-section"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Don’t request a C-section without medical indication, and avoid scheduling one just to pick a “lucky” date"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Check your yibao enrollment status before getting pregnant — even unemployed spouses can claim maternity medical expenses"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Get the “Medical Certificate of Birth” sorted out before discharge; decide on the baby’s name early and avoid typos"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Don’t skip newborn heel‑prick and hearing tests"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"Enroll your newborn in yibao right after getting the birth certificate — don’t wait until household registration is complete"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"Registering a newborn’s birth at a police station within one month"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Don’t skip that 42-day postpartum checkup — it also screens for postpartum depression"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/27-17"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"Pregnant? Don’t rehome the cat: have someone else scoop the litter daily, cook meat all the way through, and wear gloves around soil"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/27"},"children":["Chapter 27"," ·"," ","Pregnancy and childbirth: From confirming pregnancy to discharge and paperwork"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"27-03"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["03"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Getting tested for HIV, syphilis, and hepatitis B during the first prenatal visit — free prevention options available"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["During your very first prenatal checkup, you can get tested for HIV, syphilis, and hepatitis B at no personal expense. Even if results show a positive diagnosis, there are still effective ways to prevent transmission to your baby. The government offers free medication and treatment plans to block the spread of these infections from mother to child — this is known as maternal and infant transmission prevention."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost involved;"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Maternal and infant transmission is how infections pass from a mother to her unborn or newborn child. The “Wor…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Getting tested for HIV, syphilis, and hepatitis B during the first prenatal visit — free prevention options available"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost involved; the maternal and infant transmission prevention program provides these tests at no charge."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Maternal and infant transmission is how infections pass from a mother to her unborn or newborn child. The “Work Specifications for Preventing Maternal and Infant Transmission of HIV, Syphilis, and Hepatitis B (2020 Edition)” mandates that during early pregnancy or at the first prenatal visit, healthcare providers must share relevant information and “offer appropriate, standardized free testing” — meaning these three tests are completely free. Follow-up counseling and referrals are also provided based on test results. A positive diagnosis is not a dead end: Article 44 of the “Regulations on HIV/AIDS Prevention and Control” guarantees free treatment and counseling for pregnant women living with HIV to prevent transmission to their babies. Article 43 further requires that such women receive services including transmission prevention, treatment, postpartum home visits, infant follow-ups, and testing. For mothers who test positive for hepatitis B surface antigen, newborns receive both hepatitis B vaccine and hepatitis B immunoglobulin at birth (see Section 20, Item 2)."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","pro